# Who may use which topics (mosquitto.conf; SECURITY.md, "MQTT"). users.sh copies this to
# `acl` (owned by the broker, mode 0600) at every start.
#
# The server (MQTT_USERNAME, "roastwarden"): every topic, because a roaster set up with its own
# topics (docs/ingest-mapping.md) or the simulated drum (sim/drum/...) uses topics of its own.
user roastwarden
topic readwrite #

# Home Assistant (MQTT_HOME_ASSISTANT_PASSWORD; docs/home-assistant.md): reads the discovery,
# the roasters' state and the server's presence, sends its own birth message, nothing else.
user homeassistant
topic read homeassistant/#
topic read roastwarden/ha/#
topic read roastwarden/server/status
topic write homeassistant/status

# Every other user is a roaster whose name is its device id: its own telemetry, status, debug
# and commands under roaster/<id>/, and the server's presence (its heater stops when the
# server goes offline). A roaster with topics of its own needs lines of its own here, e.g.
#   user my_drum
#   topic readwrite my_drum/#
pattern readwrite roaster/%u/#
pattern read roastwarden/server/status
